  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "GStreamer is a streaming media framework based on graphs of filters which operate on media data. The gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free package contains a collection of plug-ins for GStreamer.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* gstreamer: gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free: gstreamer: heap out-of-bounds write in adpcmdec IMA/DVI ADPCM decoder (CVE-2026-19387)\n\n* gstreamer: gstreamer1-plugins-ugly-free: gstreamer: integer overflow/underflow in asfdemux bounds checks leading to out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-19389)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
